The words "to spare" seem odd to me there.  If you have it at all,
you have it to spare (unless it's the very early game and you just
plain have no *potions* to spare of any kind, but I seldom get any
scrolls identified that early).

Once you have *one* potion of unholy water, you can make any
amount of it you should happen to need.  Just double-dip a few
potions
of object detection (by far the most abundant potion in the game, due
to nymphs) into the nearest fountain (or zap them with a wand
of cancellation), then dip the resulting stack of uncursed potions of
water into the one potion of unholy water.  Voila, your one potion of
unholy water just begat several.  You can continue to produce it
indefinitely for the remainder of the game, as long as you never
use up (or otherwise lose) your last one.  Once I obtain unholy
water, I always keep at least one locked in a chest.

The tricky part is getting the one potion of unholy water to start
with.
I would be interested in discussing various strategies for obtaining
the first one, in the event you don't get lucky and fine one in a shop
or bones pile.  There are (thank goodness) very few monsters who
randomly curse your possessions until late in the game (like, often
none until Gehennom), which is clearly too long to wait.  I've heard
you can make it by praying on a cross-aligned altar, but that I've
never had the gall to attempt that.  Are there other ways?

